            <ArticleTitle>Isolated congenital absence of posterior cruciate ligament? A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12306-008-0044-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of a 28-year-old Asiatic male with the isolated absence of a posterior cruciate ligament is reported. Clinical features, diagnostic steps, therapeutic strategies and follow-up are described. A review of the literature is also presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
